## Analytic checkpoint

P73(T)'s measurable-set transfer is valid using compact subsets, without assuming the sumset itself is measurable. Put "'`B={|g−1_Ω|>δ}`, `b=|B|`, and `A=Ω'"\\B"'`. The same PD argument gives `A+A ⊂ Ω∪B`. For each compact `K⊂A`, the compact-set circle sumset theorem gives `min(1,2|K|)≤|Ω∪B|≤μ+b`. Inner regularity gives `min(1,2|A|)≤μ+b`. If `b<μ/3`, then `μ+b<2/3<1`, so saturation is impossible, and `2(μ−b)≤μ+b` is a contradiction. Thus `b≥μ/3` and the claimed bound follows. No counterexample arises from a completed-Haar measurable Ω or a nonmeasurable sumset.

A precise obstruction to P72(e)'"'s literal uniform conclusion has been found. Let "'`c=1−τ>0` and `φ_B(x)=c·1_[−1,1](x)+B(1−|x|)_+`. Each profile is bounded, supported in the stated interval, and at least c there. With `t=πξ` and `y=sin(t)/t`, its Fourier transform is `2cy cos(t)+By²≥−c²/B`. Therefore no common negative depth depending only on τ follows from the stated continuum hypotheses, which lack a common upper bound. This does not refute the intended box-bounded weighted-interval statement. Its missing compactness passage is still a GAP.

The reproducible numerical script is `adv_p72_74_scratch/audit_vm.py`. It is now running on dirichlet only. It compares both LPs for P72(a), tests complex and real PD polynomials for P73(T), and tests exact-in-formula Fourier integrals of symmetric arc unions for P74. Floating-point computations will be labeled numerical evidence, not rigorous all-x certificates.
